---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
// DRAFT
---
<Tunnel title="Clean Format | Save My Gig!" status="Quick_Fix">
  <div class="review-flag">DRAFT, review pending.</div>
  <div class="step-label">Step 4</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">Format the USB clean</h2>

  <!-- The consent for this format is collected two screens upstream on
       /backup, and its YES answer routes to /repair, not here. So the only
       screen that actually erases the drive was shipping with no warning and
       no consent on it. Every tunnel screen is a real URL with a back button,
       so arriving here without having just read /backup is normal, not an edge
       case. The warning belongs on the screen that does the damage. -->
  <div class="alert-card" style="margin:0 0 1.25rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>
      <strong>This erases the drive completely.</strong> Anything still only on
      this drive is gone. If any file failed to copy earlier, it is not coming
      back after this step.
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Confirm you are on the right disk: check the name and the size before you touch anything.</li>
    <li>Format the <em>device</em>, not the volume. On Mac: Disk Utility, View, Show All Devices.</li>
    <li>Format: <span class="mono">FAT32</span> · Scheme: <span class="mono">MBR</span> · Quick format OK.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="question">Formatted successfully?</p>

  <Choice step="qf_format"
    a={{ href: '/protocol/quick-fix/export', label: 'YES, CLEAN AND EMPTY' }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/quick-fix/fresh-usb', label: 'NO, FORMAT FAILS', desc: 'A drive that won\'t format is done. Different drive.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
